## Case Study 1: Regional Health Partners

### Organization Profile

| Attribute | Details |
|-----------|---------|
| Organization | Regional Health Partners |
| Type | Integrated health system |
| Size | 12 hospitals, 2,500 physicians |
| Location | Midwest US |
| EHR | Epic (hospitals), Athena (clinics) |
| MedSync Customer Since | March 2022 |
| Products | Core, Connect, Analytics |

### Challenge

Regional Health Partners faced significant care coordination challenges across their multi-facility network:

- **Referral Leakage**: 50% of referrals going to out-of-network providers
- **Care Gaps**: 35% of patients missing critical follow-up appointments
- **Data Silos**: Clinicians unable to see patient activity across facilities
- **Administrative Burden**: Care coordinators spending 60% of time on administrative tasks

### Solution

Regional Health Partners implemented the full MedSync platform:

| Component | Use Case |
|-----------|----------|
| MedSync Core | Centralized care coordination for 25,000 high-risk patients |
| MedSync Connect | Network-wide referral management |
| MedSync Analytics | Population health risk stratification |

### Implementation

| Phase | Timeline | Scope |
|-------|----------|-------|
| Phase 1 | Months 1-3 | Core platform, 3 pilot sites |
| Phase 2 | Months 4-6 | Epic integration, Connect rollout |
| Phase 3 | Months 7-9 | Analytics, full deployment |

### Results

| Metric | Before | After | Improvement |
|--------|--------|-------|-------------|
| In-network Referrals | 50% | 82% | +64% |
| Referral Cycle Time | 4.5 days | 1.2 days | -73% |
| Care Gap Closure | 65% | 88% | +35% |
| Admin Time Reduction | — | 45% | -45% |
| Patient Wait Time | 18 days | 8 days | -56% |
| Revenue Retained | — | $12M/year | — |

### Quote

> "MedSync has transformed how we coordinate care across our network. Our care coordinators finally have one place to manage their patients, regardless of which facility they visit. The results speak for themselves—we've reduced referral leakage by over 30 percentage points."

**— Dr. Jennifer Thompson, Chief Medical Officer**

